sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client
    participant Auth as Authorization Service
    participant Redis
    participant Fraud as Fraud Service
    participant DB as Auth DB
    participant Outbox as Outbox Publisher
    participant Kafka
    participant Ledger as Ledger Service

    Client->>Auth: POST /authorizations\n(Idempotency-Key, accountId, amount)
    Auth->>Redis: Optional idempotency/cache lookup
    Redis-->>Auth: Cache miss or prior result

    Auth->>DB: Load account + authorization state
    DB-->>Auth: Account details

    Auth->>Fraud: Risk check request
    Fraud-->>Auth: APPROVE

    Auth->>DB: Begin transaction
    Auth->>DB: Check available balance
    Auth->>DB: Reserve funds\n(available -= amount, reserved += amount)
    Auth->>DB: Insert authorization(status=AUTHORIZED)
    Auth->>DB: Insert outbox event
    Auth->>DB: Commit transaction
    DB-->>Auth: Success

    Auth-->>Client: 201 AUTHORIZED

    Outbox->>DB: Poll unsent outbox events
    DB-->>Outbox: AuthorizationCreated event
    Outbox->>Kafka: Publish authorization event
    Outbox->>DB: Mark outbox event as sent

    Kafka-->>Ledger: Consume authorization event
    Ledger->>Ledger: Idempotency/dedup check
    Ledger->>Ledger: Write immutable ledger entry / projection
    Ledger-->>Kafka: Ack